.TH "sojuctl" "1" "2026\-10\-30"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
sojuctl \- Manage a running instance of the soju IRC bouncer
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBsojuctl\fR [options.\&.\&.\&] <command.\&.\&.\&>
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
sojuctl sends a \fIBouncerServ\fR command to a running soju instance.\& See the
\fIIRC SERVICE\fR section in \fBsoju\fR(1) for more information.\&
.PP
sojuctl requires a \fIlisten unix+admin://\fR directive in the soju configuration
file.\& sojuctl needs to be run with write permissions on the soju admin socket.\&
.PP
With \fImessage\-store turso\fR, \fBturso create\-admin \-username\fR <name>
\fB\-password\fR <password> creates an administrator and their cloud database
directly, without a running server or admin socket.\& Run it before starting
soju, or restart soju afterwards to load the new account.\& Other commands
continue to use the running server'\&s admin socket.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-h, \-help\fR
.RS 4
Show help message and quit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-config\fR <path>
.RS 4
Path to the config file.\& If unset, the default config file path is used,
if any.\&
.PP
.RE
